## Confirmed VALID Findings (3 reportable)

1. **Directory Cluster Identity→Pubkey Enumeration (IDOR)** — `ds-apip`, `api`, `apip` production hosts all expose unauthenticated `GET /identity/{id}` (200/404 oracle) and `POST /identity/fetch_bulk` with CORS `*`, no rate limiting. Passively proven via GET/HEAD. CVSS ~5.3 Medium.

2. **Desktop Windows Key-Storage ACL Bypass** — `keystorage.bin` and `keystorage.password.bin` written without ACL restrictions (mode 644), allowing same-user process reads of DPAPI password + encrypted keystore. RAG-verified across 6 source files on GitHub `stable`. CVSS ~4.6-5.5 Medium.

3. **Safe-01 HSTS/Expect-CT Gap** — `OPTIONS 204` returns full HSTS + Expect-CT headers; `GET 400` omits them — byte-stable across 5 `safe-*` hosts behind 203.56.112.231. Low severity defense-in-depth.

