## Objective
- Conduct bug bounty security assessment of Threema infrastructure (directory servers, safe backup, chat, desktop source, work/broadcast/gateway) under passive-first scope constraints (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps)
- Identify and classify vulnerabilities across the Threema program surface, with browser-proven evidence where possible

## Important Details
- **Scope constraints**: `passive_first` = GET/HEAD only per `scope.yml:37-44`; all POST-derived findings are policy-gated pending operator authorization via `reports/approval-request-directory-cluster.md`
- **Triager verdicts**: `reports/valid-bugs.md` shows "VALID new/reportable: 0" with repeated HOLDs on directory-cluster leads — triager authority supersedes agent self-classification
- **Program rule**: Secrets in commits use sha256 only, never raw
- **Agent state**: `{"phase":"RECON","target":"api"}` — targeting chat/directory servers, NOT desktop
- **Model**: mimo
- **Key constraint learned**: Browsers cannot attach bodies to GET requests (fetch throws TypeError); browser-viable zero-preflight primitive is `POST + Content-Type: text/plain` (CORS-safelisted simple request)
- **KEY KB FILESYSTEM CONTRADICTION**: `poc/` directory absent for 25+ consecutive cycles despite KB claims of sha256 hashes; `reposcan-raw/threema-ch/` 18 repo dirs ALL EMPTY (0 source files); `state_bigpickle.json` = `{"phase":"POC","target":"chat"}` not "desktop" as KB claims; filesystem ground truth overrides all KB artifact assertions

